  "kernel": "89e31cdca55e39a794cee6f0d9331e90c0a28ab8",
  "kernel_repo": "Aiden-HQ/AidenHQ",
  "notes": [
    "May add authority (grants, writes, roles or secrets) in: clickhouse, glean, grafana, primer. Auto-updates accept it; turn them off to review first.",
    "A new install starts with autonomy full",
    "Sign-ins finish by pasting the loopback address, so no domain allowlist is needed",
    "The caller check, fence, reviewer, source writer and vendor proxy ship in @aidenhq/sdk",
    "Every connection connects with one click",
    "Apps-mcp and CI registration get App tokens through the kernel's codehost route",
    "Github-mcp gets every App token through the kernel's codehost route and no longer mounts the App key",
    "Ops answer the kernel only; the grant check lives in the kernel",
    "Verify-security passes on a fresh install again",
    "Aiden says where a message reached the owner as the send's result shows it",
    "The owner reaches the board signed in after setup",
    "Only a browser navigation moves from 127.0.0.1 to localhost",
    "Five upgrade polish issues from the 2026.11.2 to 2026.11.18 test",
    "An approved tool call replays as its requester at the control plane",
    "A fresh host installs the kernel's deps before it reads the pin",
    "Create_repo is Tier 0 in an org the owner allows",
    "An agent no longer configured is retired, not paused, and leaves the board",
    "The permission picker opens on what the connection already grants",
    "Wake a blocked dependent when its blocker closes",
    "Host setup changed (ops/setup.sh or ops/vm): an update runs apply only, so running the installer again may be needed (curl -fsSL https://get.aidenhq.ai | sh)."
  ],
  "release": "2026.11.18.1"
}
